<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Plantagenet</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Plantagenets, Plantagenet dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Plantagenet was a royal dynasty descended from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geoffrey-plantagenet-count-of-anjou">Geoffrey Plantagenet, Count of Anjou</a>, whose son became King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-england">Henry II of England</a> in 1154. Through inheritance and marriage Henry ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, Normandy, Anjou and Aquitaine, the so-called Angevin Empire, though his son John lost Normandy to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1204. The dynasty and its cadet branches, Lancaster and York, held the English throne until 1485.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-plantagenet.jpg" alt="House of Plantagenet" width="320" height="352" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blason_maison_Plantagen%C3%AAt.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
